 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an application for\na real property tax exemption from the Lighthouse International Christian\nGathering",
    "basePrintNo": "S9606",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9606-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9606\n\nSPONSOR: CANZONERI-FITZPATRICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an applica-\ntion for a real property tax exemption from the Lighthouse International\nChristian Gathering\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo grant a retroactive property tax exemption for the assessment roll\nfor all the 2022-2023 assessment rolls and for a portion of the\n2022-2023 school taxes and all of the 2022 and 2023 general taxes for\nthe parcel conveyed to Lighthouse International Christian Gathering\nlocated at 800 West Merrick Road, town of Hempstead, county of Nassau.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Sets forth the authorization of Nassau County to accept the\nreal property tax exemption for certain property from the Lighthouse\nInternational Christian Gathering.\n\nSection 2. Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Lighthouse International Christian Gathering is a not-for-profit,\ntax-exempt religious organization. Allowing the organization to be\nforgiven of these property tax bills will allow them to continue their\nwork in the community and keep their place of worship. This legislation\nwould allow for the Nassau County Assessor to accept an application for\na retroactive property tax exemption for the Lighthouse International\nChristian Gathering and therefore, would relieve the current fiscal\nburden on this organization.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
